{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,1]],"date-time":"2026-10-01T16:22:30Z","timestamp":1790871750963,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":46,"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","issue":"4","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2009,10,1]],"date-time":"2009-10-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1254355200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.acm.org\/publications\/policies\/copyright_policy#Background"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["dl.acm.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["ACM Trans. Model. Comput. Simul."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>\n            Halton sequences have always been quite popular with practitioners, in part because of their intuitive definition and ease of implementation. However, in their original form, these sequences have also been known for their inadequacy to integrate functions in moderate to large dimensions, in which case (\n            <jats:italic>t<\/jats:italic>\n            ,\n            <jats:italic>s<\/jats:italic>\n            )-sequences such as the Sobol' sequence are usually preferred. To overcome this problem, one possible approach is to include permutations in the definition of Halton sequences\u2014thereby obtaining\n            <jats:italic>generalized Halton sequences<\/jats:italic>\n            \u2014an idea that goes back to almost thirty years ago, and that has been studied by many researchers in the last few years. In parallel to these efforts, an important improvement in the upper bounds for the discrepancy of Halton sequences has been made by Atanassov in 2004. Together, these two lines of research have revived the interest in Halton sequences. In this article, we review different generalized Halton sequences that have been proposed recently, and compare them by means of numerical experiments. We also propose a new generalized Halton sequence which, we believe, offers a practical advantage over the surveyed constructions, and that should be of interest to practitioners.\n          <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1145\/1596519.1596520","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2009,11,4]],"date-time":"2009-11-04T18:28:31Z","timestamp":1257359311000},"page":"1-31","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1145\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":61,"title":["Generalized Halton sequences in 2008"],"prefix":"10.1145","volume":"19","author":[{"given":"Henri","family":"Faure","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institut Math\u00e9matiques de Luminy and Universit\u00e9 Paul C\u00e9zanne, Marseille cedex, France"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Christiane","family":"Lemieux","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Waterloo, ON, Canada"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"320","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2009,11,4]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_2_1_1","first-page":"15","article-title":"On the discrepancy of the Halton sequences","volume":"18","author":"Atanassov E.","year":"2004","unstructured":"Atanassov , E. 2004 . On the discrepancy of the Halton sequences . Mathematica Balkanica 18 , 15 -- 32 . Atanassov, E. 2004. On the discrepancy of the Halton sequences. Mathematica Balkanica 18, 15--32.","journal-title":"Mathematica Balkanica"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_2_1","volume-title":"Proceedings of the 5th International Conference on Numerical Methods and Applications, Borovets. Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"2542","author":"Atanassov E.","unstructured":"Atanassov , E. and Durchova , M . 2003. Generating and testing the modified Halton sequences . In Proceedings of the 5th International Conference on Numerical Methods and Applications, Borovets. Lecture Notes in Computer Science , vol. 2542 . Springer, Berlin, 91--98. Atanassov, E. and Durchova, M. 2003. Generating and testing the modified Halton sequences. In Proceedings of the 5th International Conference on Numerical Methods and Applications, Borovets. Lecture Notes in Computer Science, vol. 2542. Springer, Berlin, 91--98."},{"key":"e_1_2_2_3_1","unstructured":"Bach E. and Shallit J. 1996. Algorithmic Number Theory. Vol. 1. MIT Press Cambridge MA.   Bach E. and Shallit J. 1996. Algorithmic Number Theory. Vol. 1. MIT Press Cambridge MA."},{"key":"e_1_2_2_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0021-9991(79)90019-6"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.21314\/JCF.1997.005"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_6_1","volume-title":"Proceedings of the Conference on Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence. 72--81","author":"Cheng J.","unstructured":"Cheng , J. and Druzdzel , M . 2000. Computational investigation of low-discrepancy sequences in simulation algorithms for bayesian networks . In Proceedings of the Conference on Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence. 72--81 . Cheng, J. and Druzdzel, M. 2000. Computational investigation of low-discrepancy sequences in simulation algorithms for bayesian networks. In Proceedings of the Conference on Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence. 72--81."},{"key":"e_1_2_2_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.matcom.2005.03.004"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_8_1","volume-title":"Discr\u00e9pance de suites associ\u00e9es \u00e0 un syst\u00e8me de num\u00e9ration. Comptes Rendus Mathematique 286-A","author":"Faure H.","unstructured":"Faure , H. 1978. Discr\u00e9pance de suites associ\u00e9es \u00e0 un syst\u00e8me de num\u00e9ration. Comptes Rendus Mathematique 286-A , Acadamy of Science , Paris , 293--296. Faure, H. 1978. Discr\u00e9pance de suites associ\u00e9es \u00e0 un syst\u00e8me de num\u00e9ration. Comptes Rendus Mathematique 286-A, Acadamy of Science, Paris, 293--296."},{"key":"e_1_2_2_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4064\/aa-41-4-337-351"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF01559392"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0022-314X(92)90107-Z"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4064\/aa117-2-2"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/3-540-31186-6_8"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_14_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF01386213"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_15_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1145\/264029.264064"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_16_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jco.2005.10.004"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_17_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"L'Ecuyer P. and Lemieux C. 2002. Recent advances in randomized quasi-Monte Carlo methods. In Modeling Uncertainty: An Examination of Stochastic Theory Methods and Applications M. Dror P. L'Ecuyer and F. Szidarovszki Eds. Kluwer Academic Publishers Boston 419--474.  L'Ecuyer P. and Lemieux C. 2002. Recent advances in randomized quasi-Monte Carlo methods. In Modeling Uncertainty: An Examination of Stochastic Theory Methods and Applications M. Dror P. L'Ecuyer and F. Szidarovszki Eds. Kluwer Academic Publishers Boston 419--474.","DOI":"10.1007\/0-306-48102-2_20"},{"key":"e_1_2_2_18_1","volume-title":"Proceedings of the Conference on Monte Carlo and Quasi-Monte Carlo Methods, K.-T. Fang, F. J. Hickernell, and H. Niederreiter, Eds. Springer, 331--344","author":"Lemieux C.","unstructured":"Lemieux , C. and Owen , A . 2001. Quasi-regression and the relative importance of the ANOVA components of a function . In Proceedings of the Conference on Monte Carlo and Quasi-Monte Carlo Methods, K.-T. Fang, F. J. Hickernell, and H. Niederreiter, Eds. Springer, 331--344 . Lemieux, C. and Owen, A. 2001. Quasi-regression and the relative importance of the ANOVA components of a function. In Proceedings of the Conference on Monte Carlo and Quasi-Monte Carlo Methods, K.-T. Fang, F. J. Hickernell, and H. Niederreiter, Eds. Springer, 331--344."},{"key":"e_1_2_2_19_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1515\/mcma.2004.10.3-4.435"},{"key":"e_